{:edb/db-before-t 2482 :edb/db-after-t 2483 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535795 50 #inst "2026-10-09T07:21:39.312Z" 13194139535795 true] [17592186119721 1020 #edb/ref 17592186366635 13194139535795 true] [17592186119721 1020 #edb/ref 17592186366642 13194139535795 true] [17592186119722 1020 #edb/ref 17592186366628 13194139535795 true] [17592186119806 1020 #edb/ref 17592186366649 13194139535795 true] [17592186120120 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535795 true] [17592186120120 1100 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{33}?$" 13194139535795 true] [17592186120120 1100 "$A = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nIf $A = LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ given above, what is the value of $l_{21} \\cdot u_{33}$?" 13194139535795 false] [17592186120120 1145 "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ \\,\\,2\\,\\, & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+1{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ \\,\\,2\\,\\, & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ \\,\\,2\\,\\, & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & \\,3\\, & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{21}=2$ and ${u}_{33}=-3,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{33}=2\\cdot (-3)=-6.\n$$" 13194139535795 true] [17592186366628 1017 #edb/ref 17592186366629 13194139535795 true] [17592186366628 1089 "q-105550" 13194139535795 true] [17592186366628 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535795 true] [17592186366628 1100 "$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 6 & -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\boxed{} & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -10\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of the entry ${l}_{31}$ in the matrix $L?$" 13194139535795 true] [17592186366628 1113 #uuid "b6e8681a-9965-5403-9903-63c3dc77e9ab" 13194139535795 true] [17592186366628 1145 "We want to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{31}$ using Gaussian elimination. To do this, we take the $3$rd row of $A,$ and we add the $1$st row of $A$ multiplied by $-2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 6 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe entry ${l}_{31}$ of the matrix $L$ is the factor next to ${R}_{1},$ taken with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{l}_{31}=-(-2)=2.\n$$" 13194139535795 true] [17592186366629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366630 13194139535795 true] [17592186366629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366631 13194139535795 true] [17592186366629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366632 13194139535795 true] [17592186366629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366633 13194139535795 true] [17592186366629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366634 13194139535795 true] [17592186366629 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535795 true] [17592186366629 1041 "selection" 13194139535795 true] [17592186366629 1104 #edb/ref 17592186366630 13194139535795 true] [17592186366629 1110 #uuid "17bc7324-e64b-5010-b293-099a8b4da700" 13194139535795 true] [17592186366630 1034 "2" 13194139535795 t